{"t": 1792881390052, "cmd": "note", "args": ["--shot", "feed_double_count", "Hunger readouts disagree with 'You fed N' (#410). Tick 217390: banner '7 members hungry: all here', button 'Feed Residents (7 hungry)', click -> 'You fed 7 residents in the Town of Yellowton' (apples 15->8). The very next frame the banner says '4 members hungry: all here' and the button 'Feed Residents (4 hungry)' (shot feed13.png). Second click at 217562 -> 'You fed 4 residents' (apples 8->4). That is 11 feedings in 172 ticks for a settlement whose nameplate says '8 here, 9/20 residents', so at least 3 people were reported as fed while still hungry. Expected: after 'You fed 7' those 7 are no longer hungry (or the message says they are still hungry / need more), and the hungry count never exceeds the residents present. Same pattern at tick 206038 (fed 6, then 3 more, with 8 here)."]}
